# Networking Standards

- Every published port has its own bind variable. Never reintroduce a single shared `BIND_ADDRESS`.
  - `API_BIND_ADDRESS` (api), `WEB_BIND_ADDRESS` (web), `POSTGRES_BIND_ADDRESS`, `REDIS_BIND_ADDRESS`, `MINIO_BIND_ADDRESS`.
  - All default to `127.0.0.1` in `compose.yaml`, `.env.example`, and `.env`.
- Postgres, Redis, and MinIO/RustFS must NEVER be exposed to the LAN. Do not set their bind variables to `0.0.0.0`, and do not derive them from `API_BIND_ADDRESS`.
- Physical mobile device testing: set ONLY `API_BIND_ADDRESS=0.0.0.0` (optionally `WEB_BIND_ADDRESS=0.0.0.0`), then run `docker compose up -d` to refresh bindings. Revert afterwards.
- After any port/bind change, run `docker compose ps` and confirm Postgres/Redis still show `127.0.0.1`.
- Storage (RustFS) stays behind `--profile storage`, private bucket by default; serve files via signed URLs or a scoped public prefix, never `bucket/*`.
- Do not hide failures with `|| true`.
